## The pass-chart fragment: the same pass_chart_html the page embeds,
## regenerated each report cycle into pass-chart.txt so the open page's
## javascript can refetch the panel (a pass completes and the chart moves
## on to the next one; a pass sliding into the elements' validity window
## unhides a panel that first-painted hidden).  Named .txt so the *.html
## validator cron never sees a bare fragment.  Empty when no capable
## $sky_page serves the report OR no configured satellite has a visible
## pass -- the javascript hides the panel on a deliberate empty and keeps
## the chart it has on a failed fetch.  Deliberately NO #errorCatcher: an
## unexpected failure must fail this template (weewxd logs it and the old
## fragment stays on disk), never write error text the javascript would
## inject into the page.
#encoding UTF-8
#if $sky_page
## The page's plate, resolved exactly as index.html.tmpl resolves it, so
## a refetched chart can never disagree with the page it lands in.
## Guarded (an unknown theme raises) so a typo costs the plate, not the
## fragment: this template deliberately has no #errorCatcher.
#set $palette = 'night'
#try
#set $palette = 'light' if str($sky_page.theme($almanac)) == 'light' else 'night'
#except
#pass
#end try
$sky_page.pass_chart_html($almanac, palette=$palette)#slurp
#end if
